REM demo_hello.duck - the ONLY payload shipped with badhid-suite.
REM
REM It is a harmless proof-of-life: it waits for the host to settle, then
REM types one benign echo line and presses Enter. Its entire purpose is to
REM confirm the HID gadget + runner work end to end. It does nothing to the
REM target beyond echoing text into whatever window has focus.
REM
REM Write your OWN payloads as separate .duck files in this directory, and
REM point them only at hardware you own or are authorized to test. This suite
REM intentionally ships no offensive payloads.
REM
REM Supported here: REM, STRING, STRINGLN, ENTER + named keys, modifier
REM combos (e.g. GUI r / CTRL ALT DELETE), DELAY <ms>, DEFAULTDELAY <ms>,
REM REPEAT <n>. See README.md.

DELAY 800
STRINGLN echo badhid demo - hello from your own lab device
